        <summary class="flex items-center gap-3 pb-3 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" d="M9 6h11M9 12h11M9 18h11M4.5 6h.01M4.5 12h.01M4.5 18h.01" /></svg>
          <span class="font-bold text-gray-900">In This Guide</span>
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400">11 sections</span>
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-auto text-gray-500 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6 15l6-6 6 6" /></svg>
        </summary>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-6">
              <a href="#price-tiers" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">1.</span><span>The Short Answer</span></a>
              <a href="#unit-prices" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">2.</span><span>Cost Without Installation</span></a>
              <a href="#install-items" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">3.</span><span>Installation Cost</span></a>
              <a href="#what-moves-price" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">4.</span><span>Why Quotes Vary</span></a>
              <a href="#right-size" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">5.</span><span>What Size You Need</span></a>
              <a href="#ownership" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">6.</span><span>Running and Upkeep Cost</span></a>
              <a href="#alternatives" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">7.</span><span>Cheaper Alternatives</span></a>
              <a href="#lower-quote" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">8.</span><span>How to Lower a Quote</span></a>
              <a href="#worth-it" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">9.</span><span>Is It Worth It?</span></a>
              <a href="#mistakes" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">10.</span><span>Common Mistakes</span></a>
              <a href="#faq" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">11.</span><span>FAQ</span></a>
        </nav>
      </details>
    </div>

    <!-- Body -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          The figure that surprises most buyers is how little of a Generac standby invoice goes to the generator. Of a typical $10,000 to $20,000 installed total, the machine is often a third to a half. The balance pays for a transfer switch, an electrician, a gas fitter, a pad and permits, and sometimes a propane tank or a larger gas meter. Once you can name those pieces, you can read any quote and see where it can shrink.
        </p>

        <TopPick />

        <div id="price-tiers" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Generac Generator Cost: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            Budget $10,000 to $16,000 for the most common choice, a Guardian 22kW connected to existing natural gas, and $10,000 to $20,000 for whole-home standby in general. Homeowners and dealers commonly report straightforward 22kW jobs clustering around $12,000 to $15,000. A workable rule: take the unit price, add roughly the same again for installation, then plan on some upkeep every year. The installed ranges below are typical at the time of writing, and local labor and site conditions shift them a lot.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">System</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Typical output</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Typical unit only</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Typical installed total</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Usually covers</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Portable plus transfer switch or interlock</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">3-8kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$1,000-$1,300 (GP8000E)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$1,500-$3,500</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Selected essential circuits, manual start</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Guardian 10-14kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">10-14kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$3,200-$5,000</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$7,000-$11,000</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Essentials plus some comfort loads, maybe one AC</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Guardian 18-22kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">18-22kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$4,900-$6,500</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$10,000-$16,000</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Most homes, including a central AC with load management</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Guardian 24-26kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">24-26kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$6,500-$7,800</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$12,000-$19,000</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Larger homes, two AC systems with load management</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Protector liquid-cooled</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">30-60kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$13,000-$25,000+</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$20,000-$40,000+</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Very large or all-electric homes, light commercial</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Which tier do most homeowners land in?</h3>

          <p>
            The 18 to 22kW band. That is where the typical house with one or two central air systems ends up once a dealer runs the numbers, and it is why the 22kW figure shows up in so many quotes. The total rises fast when the job needs a long gas run, a propane tank installed from nothing, a panel or meter upgrade, or awkward site work.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What does a quote far from these ranges mean?</h3>

          <p>
            A bid well under the pattern above usually omits something, so ask what is excluded before you get excited. A bid well over it deserves an itemized breakdown, line by line, before you sign anything. Section 3 lists every line you should expect to see.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="unit-prices" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. How Much Does a Generac Generator Cost Without Installation?
          </h2>

          <p>
            A Guardian standby unit alone typically runs about $3,200 for the 10kW up to $7,800 for the 24 to 26kW models, with the liquid-cooled Protector line far higher. Treat those unit-only numbers as a guide: Generac sells standby generators through authorized dealers, and plenty of dealers will only quote an installed price. Regional differences and promotions can move the figures below by 10 to 15 percent or more.
          </p>

          <p>
            It also helps to know that the Generac name covers three quite different product families. The portable generators are retail items you can pick up from a store shelf. The air-cooled Guardian standby units are the backbone of home backup: mounted permanently outside and wired to an automatic transfer switch. At the top sit the liquid-cooled Protector generators and the PWRcell battery systems.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Model</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Rated output (LP / NG)</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Typical unit price</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Guardian 10kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">10kW / 9kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$3,200-$4,200</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Guardian 14kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">14kW / 14kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$4,200-$5,000</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Guardian 18kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">18kW / 17kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$4,900-$5,700</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Guardian 22kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">22kW / 19.5kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$5,500-$6,500</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Guardian 24-26kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Up to 26kW on LP</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$6,500-$7,800</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Protector QS liquid-cooled</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">30-60kW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$13,000-$25,000+</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">GP8000E portable</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">8,000W running</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$1,000-$1,300</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Why is a Generac rated lower on natural gas?</h3>

          <p>
            Air-cooled standby engines produce less power on natural gas than on propane, which is why the table lists two ratings. In practice a 22kW Guardian behaves like a 19.5kW machine on a natural gas line. Size your home right up to a model's propane rating, then feed it natural gas, and the safety margin you thought you had is gone.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Why is the 22kW such a popular size?</h3>

          <p>
            Because prices do not climb in a straight line. Moving from 14 to 18 to 22kW costs relatively little, since those units share much of the same design, so the 22kW buys a lot of extra capacity for a modest premium. The largest air-cooled sizes, and above all the liquid-cooled Protector units, cost disproportionately more for each added kilowatt.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Is the transfer switch included in the unit price?</h3>

          <p>
            Sometimes. Generac bundles the transfer switch with some generators and sells it separately with others. A 200-amp whole-house automatic transfer switch commonly adds about $600 to $1,500 for the hardware alone, and service-rated or smart-management versions cost more. When you compare unit prices, check that each one either includes the switch or leaves it out, so the comparison is fair.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="install-items" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. How Much Does Generac Installation Cost?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Installation typically costs about as much as the generator itself, and on a difficult site it costs more. This is the part of the bill that varies most and catches homeowners off guard. A standby generator is a small construction project that touches electrical work, gas work and sometimes structural work, and each of those needs its own permit and inspection. A capable dealer coordinates the whole thing, and every trade on site shows up on your invoice.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-4">Typical 22kW Install, Rough Shares</p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-center">
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">40-50%</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Generator unit</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#38BDF8]">10-15%</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Automatic transfer switch</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">25-35%</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Electrical and gas labor</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#38BDF8]">5-10%</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Pad, permits, startup, misc</p>
              </div>
            </div>
